  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "People complained about the (arguably dumb) 4k resolution limit for the config file. Now we have (an equally dumb) 8k limit on the config file. There's no reason for it to exist - people with beefier GPUs like 6800XT or 3090 can easily take 16k screenshots and barely notice them, assuming that off-thread encoding is implemented properly like in the mod. Discord generates previews just fine for up to 12k screenshots. File size, which indeed can be hundreds of megabyes for 16k PNGs, is also not a concern for some people (or, you know, we can get a jpeg option).\nPeople whose hardware can't handle higher resolution, be it quest or a weaker PC, now have the new lower-res options, so \"I accidentally broke my config\" is not even a real usability issue.\nSo, why can't we have nice things? Why does VRChat continue to add or maintain more restrictions in places where they make absolutely zero sense?",
